-<section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The honest version</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">What down payment help is, and is not</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Down payment assistance on the Grand Strand comes from state and agency programs with their own rules, income limits, and trade-offs. Our lending partner, <a href="https://brickwoodmortgage.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">BrickWood Mortgage</a>, does not offer its own down payment assistance program, and we would rather tell you that plainly. Closing costs are the other half of cash-to-close; estimate them with the <a href="/buyers/closing-costs/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">closing costs calculator</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">What we do: when a program fits you, we help you weigh it honestly, because assistance sometimes arrives with a higher rate or price adjustments that cost more over time than the help is worth. Sometimes the program is the right call. Sometimes a smaller house or a longer save is. We run the numbers both ways and show you.</p></div></section><section id="afba" style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Required disclosure</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Affiliated Business Arrangement Disclosure</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Chapter3 Realty Corp has a business relationship with BrickWood Mortgage (NMLS #189497). Because of this relationship, referrals to BrickWood Mortgage may provide Chapter3 Realty a financial or other benefit.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You are NOT required to use BrickWood Mortgage as a condition for the purchase, sale, or refinance of any property. There are frequently other settlement service providers available with similar services. You are free to shop around to determine that you are receiving the best services and the best rate for those services.</p></div></section>
-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.5rem 1.5rem 4rem"><p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem">Common Questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Frequently asked questions</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What down payment assistance exists in South Carolina?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">SC Housing offers statewide programs, including forgivable down payment assistance for eligible buyers, alongside county-level options. Eligibility ties to income limits, credit score, and purchase price caps that change periodically.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Do assistance programs work in Horry County?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Yes. SC Housing programs cover Horry County purchases that meet program limits, and Myrtle Beach buyers use them regularly with FHA, VA, USDA, and conventional loans.</p></div></div></section>
-</main>
-<section style="background:var(--navy)"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;padding:3rem 1.5rem"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.9rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:.8rem">Talk to a licensed Grand Strand agent.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.6);max-width:560px;margin:0 auto 1.6rem;line-height:1.7">Get straight answers on pricing, neighborhoods, and the financing that fits, from a licensed local agent.</p><div style="display:flex;gap:.75rem;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Speak to a Licensed Agent</a></div></div></section><footer>
+<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">SC Down Payment Help</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Buying a home</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Down payment help in Horry County:<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">you do not have to be a <span style="white-space:nowrap">first-time buyer.</span></em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 1, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">SC Housing gives an eligible buyer $10,000. Most houses for sale in Conway, Loris, Aynor and Longs are under its price limit. Across the beach towns, about a third are.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The $10,000 is a second mortgage from SC Housing, the state's housing agency, and it pays toward the down payment and closing costs. SC Housing forgives it after you have lived in the home 15 years. If you sell, refinance or move out sooner, you repay all of it, from the sale or the new loan.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">To qualify, a household of one or two can earn up to $114,960, or $134,120 for three or more. The home can cost up to $450,000, you need a credit score of 640, and you must own no other property when the loan closes.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Homes that fit SC Housing's limits, sent to you</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Get the list</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#qualify" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Do you qualify</a></li><li><a href="#paying-it-back" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Paying it back</a></li><li><a href="#which-homes" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Which homes</a></li><li><a href="#no-money-down" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">No money down</a></li><li><a href="#which-program" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Which program</a></li><li><a href="#local-help" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Local help</a></li><li><a href="#how-to-apply" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">How to apply</a></li><li><a href="#sc-housing-questions" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;c