+                <li>An interview to learn more about your family's story, housing needs, and homeownership goals</li>
+              </ul>
+              <details class="hfh-more">
+                <summary>More about the selection process</summary>
+                <div class="hfh-more-body">
+                  <p>Our Family Selection Committee is a dedicated group of community volunteers who help ensure our selection process is fair, thoughtful, and mission-centered. During the home visit and interview, the committee seeks to better understand each family's current housing situation and evaluate the applicant's demonstrated need for affordable housing and willingness to partner with Habitat through the Homebuyer Program.</p>
+                  <p>At the same time, Habitat staff complete a detailed financial review to determine each applicant's ability to pay an affordable mortgage, ensuring the home remains financially sustainable for the family over the long term. Habitat affiliates commonly evaluate applicants using the three core criteria of need, willingness to partner, and ability to repay an affordable mortgage.</p>
+                  <p>After all home visits, interviews, and financial reviews have been completed, the Family Selection Committee thoughtfully reviews the information gathered and votes to recommend the family or families who they believe are the best fit for that specific homeownership opportunity.</p>
+                  <p>Families who are not selected are encouraged to continue participating in Financial Mentorship. As additional homes become available through Habitat's land strategy and construction schedule, there will be future opportunities to apply.</p>
+                </div>
+              </details>
+            </div>
+          </li>
+
+          <!-- Step 5 -->
+          <li class="hfh-step">
+            <span class="hfh-step-num" aria-hidden="true">5</span>
+            <div class="hfh-step-card">
+              <span class="hfh-step-label">Step 5</span>
+              <h3>Homebuyer in Process (HIP)</h3>
+              <p>Congratulations! Once selected, you'll officially become a Homebuyer in Process (HIP) and begin partnering with Habitat through our structured Homebuyer Program. As a Homebuyer in Process, you'll continue preparing for homeownership by:</p>
+              <ul class="hfh-checks one-col">
+                <li>Completing required Sweat Equity hours</li>
+                <li>Meeting regularly with your Financial Mentor</li>
+                <li>Attending monthly Financial Literacy Classes</li>
+                <li>Participating in Quarterly Homebuyer Workshops</li>
+                <li>Building your required savings and maintaining financial readiness</li>
+                <li>Working alongside Habitat staff and volunteers as your future home is prepared</li>
+              </ul>
+              <p>During this stage, we'll continue walking alongside you to ensure you feel confident and prepared for the responsibilities of homeownership.</p>
+            </div>
+          </li>
+
+          <!-- Step 6 -->
+          <li class="hfh-step">
+            <span class="hfh-step-num" aria-hidden="true">6</span>
+            <div class="hfh-step-card">
+              <span class="hfh-step-label">Step 6</span>
+              <h3>Welcome Home</h3>
+              <p>When construction is complete and you've met all program requirements, you'll receive the keys to your new home. <a href="#hfh-welcome" style="color:var(--hfh-blue-text);font-weight:700;text-decoration:underline;">See what that looks like ↓</a></p>
+            </div>
+          </li>
+
+        </ol>
+      </div>
+    </div>
+  </section>
+
+  <!-- ===================== 5. SUCCESS ===================== -->
+  <section class="hfh-gray hfh-success" id="hfh-welcome">
+    <div class="hfh-wrap hfh-split">
+      <div class="hfh-photo-wrap">
+        <div class="hfh-photo">
+          <img decoding="async" src="https://habitathorry.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/484826225_1069858261840454_5500156117437342420_n.jpg" alt="A new Habitat homeowner holding the keys to their home" loading="lazy">
+        </div>
+      </div>
+      <div>
+        <span class="hfh-eyebrow">Step 6 · Welcome Home</span>
+        <h2>It's Time to Celebrate!</h2>
+        <p>When construction is complete and you've successfully met all program requirements, you'll receive the keys to your new home during your Home Dedication Ceremony, surrounded by the volunteers, sponsors, staff, and community members who helped make your homeownership journey possible.</p>
+        <p><strong>But your partnership with Habitat doesn't end there.</strong> As a Habitat homeowner, you'll continue to have access to resources, educational opportunities, homeowner support, and a community that's invested in your long-term success.</p>
+        <p class="hfh-quote">At Habitat for Humanity of Horry County, we don't just build houses—we build hope, lasting partnerships, stronger communities, and brighter futures.</p>
+      </div>
+    </div>
+  </section>
+
+  <!-- ===================== 6. WHO CAN APPLY ===================== -->
+  <section>
+    <div class="hfh-wrap">
+      <div class="hfh-narrow hfh-center">
+        <span class="hfh-eyebrow">Who Can Apply?</span>
+        <h2>Basic Eligibility</h2>
+        <p class="hfh-lead">To be considered for Habitat's Homebuyer Program, applicants must meet the following requirements.</p>
+      </div>
+      <div class="hfh-two">
+        <div class="hfh-card">
+          <h3>Applicants must:</h3>
+          <ul class="hfh-checks one-col">
+            <li>Have lived in Horry County for at least 12 months</li>
+            <li>Be a U.S. Citizen or Legal Permanent Resident</li>
+            <li>Meet Habitat's income guidelines (35–80% Area Median Income)</li>
+            <li>Demonstrate a need for safe, decent, affordable housing</li>
+            <li>Be willing to partner with Habitat</li>
+          </ul>
+        </div>
+        <div class="hfh-card hfh-card-blue">
+          <h3>Income Guidelines</h3>
+          <p>To be eligible for Habitat's Homebuyer Program, applicants must meet our household income guidelines. Our program serves households earning approximately:</p>
+          <div class="hfh-ami">35%–80%</div>
+          <span class="hfh-ami-label">of Area Median Income (AMI)</span>
+          <!-- Income guidelines flyer (PDF) – opens in a new tab -->
+          <a class="hfh-btn hfh-btn-white" href="https://habitathorry.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/2026-6-8-Homebuyer-Program-Flyer-1.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View Current Income Guidelines</a>
+          <p class="hfh-small">Not sure if you qualify? We encourage you to <a href="https://form.jotform.com/262364906777066">connect with a Financial Mentor</a>. We're happy to help you understand the income guidelines and discuss your path toward homeownership.</p>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+    </div>
+  </section>
+
+  <!-- ===================== 7. FAQ ===================== -->
+  <section class="hfh-gray">
+    <div class="hfh-wrap">
+      <div class="hfh-narrow">
+        <div class="hfh-center">
+          <span class="hfh-eyebrow">Questions?</span>
+          <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
+        </div>
+        <div class="hfh-faq">
+
+          <details>
+            <summary>When do homeownership opportunities become available?</summary>
+            <div class="hfh-ans">
+              <p>Habitat builds homes according to our land strategy and construction schedule, so homeownership opportunities become available throughout the year as new homes are planned. Approximately six months before construction begins, we invite participants actively engaged in Financial Mentorship to apply for those specific homes.</p>
+            </div>
+          </details>
+
+          <details>
+            <summary>How do I get started?</summary>
+            <div class="hfh-ans">
+              <p>Your journey begins with Financial Mentorship.</p>
+              <p>We'll pair you with a volunteer Financial Mentor who will work alongside you to build your financial confidence, strengthen your credit and savings, and help prepare you for homeownership. As future homeownership opportunities become available, active Financial Mentorship participants receive priority consideration to apply.</p>
+              <a class="hfh-btn hfh-btn-primary" href="https://form.jotform.com/262364906777066">Get a Financial Mentor</a>
+            </div>
+          </details>
+
+          <details>
+            <summary>How long does the Homebuyer Program take?</summary>
+            <div class="hfh-ans">
+              <p>Every family's journey is unique.</p>
+              <p>Once accepted into the Homebuyer Program, most families complete the program in approximately 6–18 months, depending on the home opportunity, construction schedule, and individual progress toward program milestones.</p>
+              <p>Our goal isn't simply to help you purchase a home—it's to ensure you're prepared for long-term success as a homeowner.</p>
+            </div>
+          </details>
+
+          <details>
+            <summary>Can I choose which home I receive?</summary>
+            <div class="hfh-ans">
+              <p>Homeownership opportunities are based on Habitat's current land strategy and construction schedule. As homes become available, we invite applicants to apply for specific homes that best fit their household size, needs, and readiness.</p>
+            </div>
+          </details>
+
+          <details>
+            <summary>What if I'm not selected?</summary>
+            <div class="hfh-ans">
+              <p>Not being selected for one homeownership opportunity does not mean your journey with Habitat has ended.</p>
+              <p>We encourage you to continue partnering with your Financial Mentor, building your savings, completing educational opportunities, and preparing for homeownership. As additional homes become available, there will be future opportunities to apply.</p>
+              <p>Our hope is to help every family become homeownership ready, and we'll continue walking alongside you every step of the way.</p>
+            </div>
+          </details>
+
+          <details>
+            <summary>How are families selected?</summary>
+            <div class="hfh-ans">
+              <p>Every application is reviewed through Habitat's Family Selection process.</p>
+              <p>Habitat staff evaluates each applicant's ability to pay an affordable mortgage, while our volunteer Family Selection Committee conducts home visits and interviews to better understand each family's housing needs and willingness to partner with Habitat.</p>
+              <p>Together, these perspectives help ensure a fair, thoughtful, and mission-driven selection process.</p>
+            </div>
+          </details>
+
+          <details>
+            <summary>What makes Habitat different from buying a home on the open market?</summary>
+            <div class="hfh-ans">
+              <p>Habitat isn't just building houses—we're preparing homeowners.</p>
+              <p>Through Financial Mentorship, homebuyer education, Sweat Equity, and ongoing support, we partner with families long before they receive the keys to their home. Our goal is to equip every homeowner with the knowledge, confidence, and resources needed to thrive for years to come.</p>
+            </div>
+          </details>
+
+          <details>
+            <summary>I'm not ready yet. Can Habitat still help me?</summary>
+            <div class="hfh-ans">
+              <p><strong>Absolutely.</strong></p>
+              <p>You don't have to wait until you're "ready" to begin your journey. Whether you're working on your credit, building savings, paying down debt, or simply exploring the idea of homeownership, we'd love to partner with you.</p>
+              <p>Your first step is connecting with a Financial Mentor—and your journey can begin today.</p>
+              <a class="hfh-btn hfh-btn-primary" href="https://form.jotform.com/262364906777066">Get a Financial Mentor</a>
+            </div>
+          </details>
+
+        </div>
+      </div>
+    </div>
+  </section>
